+# Design
+
+## Context
+
+Two adjacent `///` doc blocks got welded together by a merge, and rustdoc binds a doc comment to
+the item directly below it. The fix is to re-split the fused blocks so each documents its own
+function. No code, signatures, ordering, or formatting change — only which comment lines sit above
+which function. See proposal.md for motivation.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:**
+- Each of the four affected functions (`addressable_scope`, `repository_scope`, `assign_schema`,
+  `synthesize_schema`) carries exactly the doc block written for it.
+- Edits are comments-only: no code line changes, no reformatting, no changes outside the two files.
+
+**Non-Goals:**
+- No new doc text is authored for functions that end up undocumented.
+- No reordering of functions; functions stay in their current file order.
+
+## Decisions
+
+**Split the fused block on the semantic seam, not at an arbitrary line.** In
+`apps/cli/src/commands/execution/mod.rs` the block above `repository_scope` currently contains TWO
+documented items concatenated:
+- `addressable_scope`'s block ends at the `# Errors` paragraph
+  ("`[`Failure`] when `execution` is not a valid identifier.`") — it takes an `execution` arg and
+  returns `Result`.
+- `repository_scope`'s block begins at "The same addressing rule as [`addressable_scope`]… One home
+  for the workspace and project literals…" and correctly ends above `fn repository_scope`.
+
+The `# Errors` heading belongs to `addressable_scope` (it is the only one returning a `Result`), so
+that is the cut line. Move the `addressable_scope` portion (through the `# Errors` line) to directly
+above `fn addressable_scope`; leave the `repository_scope` portion where it is.
+
+**Keep `assign_schema`'s loss honest.** In `apps/cli/src/commands/mcp/tools.rs`, the "Closed like
+every other schema here… `serve::routes::synthesize` … `start_schema`" block clearly documents the
+synthesize path (it names `fixture`, `route`, and the synthesize server route). It currently sits
+above `assign_schema`. Move it to directly above `fn synthesize_schema`. `assign_schema` then has
+no doc block; we do NOT invent one, consistent with the "comments only" constraint.
+
+*Alternatives considered:* (a) reorder the functions so their natural docs fall into place —
+rejected, because reordering touches code position, not just comments. (b) add new doc blocks for
+the now-undocumented functions — rejected, out of the stated scope.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- [Cutting the fused block at the wrong line] → the `# Errors` heading is the unambiguous anchor
+  (only `addressable_scope` returns a `Result`); verify after editing that `repository_scope` has
+  no `# Errors` and `addressable_scope` does.
+- [A stray blank/contiguous `///` line leaving two blocks still merged] → rustdoc still treats all
+  consecutive `///` lines as one block; the moved block must end with a blank line before the next
+  function's block starts. Verify by reading the final region.
